---
import GameLayout from '../layouts/GameLayout.astro';
import '../styles/trust-pages.css';
---
<GameLayout title="About EMFLS Games | Original Browser Games" description="Learn what EMFLS Games is, how its original browser games are designed, and what you can expect when you play." canonical="/about/" robots="index, follow" ogType="website">
  <div class="trust-page"><div class="container trust-page__inner">
    <header class="trust-page__header"><p class="trust-page__eyebrow">About</p><h1>About EMFLS Games</h1><p class="trust-page__lead">EMFLS Games is a collection of original browser games designed for quick play on phones and desktop browsers.</p></header>
    <div class="trust-page__content">
      <section class="trust-section"><h2>What EMFLS Games is</h2><p>EMFLS Games brings original browser games together in one place for direct, low-friction play. No install or account is required, and each game is built around a short session that is easy to understand.</p></section>
      <section class="trust-section about-mechanics"><h2>How the mechanics differ</h2><p>The eight games do not share a reskinned ruleset. Pulse Junction judges one timed tap; Mirror Drift reflects one drag into a paired route; Gravity Pact moves both players’ tokens on a shared board; Orbit Slip combines automatic orbit with radius control. Twin Ledger balances signed values, Signal Sweep applies a visual rule, Field Bloom checks exact grid activations, and Glass Bloom asks when to bank an exposed pot.</p><p>Each game’s rules and scoring are implemented in its own browser game, and the game pages describe how their specific mechanic works.</p></section>
      <section class="trust-section"><h2>Controls and browser use</h2><p>The games run in the browser and do not require an install or account. Input differs by mechanic: some games use taps or dragging, some provide keyboard controls, and some offer both. Each game page lists its supported controls and scoring before the related-game links, so you can check the interaction before starting.</p></section>
      <section class="trust-panel"><h2>Keep playing</h2><p>Choose a game and start a quick session, or send feedback if something could work better.</p><div class="trust-actions"><a class="button" href="/games/">Browse Games</a><a class="button button--secondary" href="/contact/">Contact</a></div></section>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</GameLayout>
